1. In the process of transporting the refrigerator, try to keep the refrigerator upright, the tilt angle must be less than 45 degrees;
2. The refrigerator should be placed away from heat source, avoid direct sunlight, keep good air circulation and dry degree;
3. In order to minimize the running noise of the refrigerator, the bottom adjusting feet should be properly adjusted to keep the refrigerator horizontal and tilt slightly forward. At the same time, the space between the box and the wall should be about 10cm;
4. The refrigerator should be cleaned during daily use to avoid bacteria breeding and peculiar smell inside the box. When cleaning the refrigerator, first disconnect the power cord, then clean it with warm water and a little detergent, and then wipe it with clean water;
5. Use a socket with a separate grounding wire. If the metal parts of the refrigerator have a tingling sensation during use, stop using it immediately;
6. Do not store too much food in the daily use of the refrigerator, otherwise it will hinder the air circulation in the box, resulting in the increase of power consumption of the refrigerator and a long time without shutdown. It is recommended to use at most 70% of the space in the refrigerator;
7. To prolong the service life of the refrigerator, please do not often stop using the refrigerator.

1. Before refrigerating or freezing food, it is necessary to ensure the freshness, cleanliness and hygiene of food materials, and pay attention to the shelf life of food, so as to avoid bacteria breeding and food spoilage caused by storing for too long;
2. For foods with special smell or easy to spoil, seal them with plastic wrap before storing them in the refrigerator to avoid food odors or contaminating the inner container; 
3. Food with high moisture content also needs to be sealed with plastic wrap, otherwise the food will easily lose moisture and cause frost or condensation inside the box; 
4. Raw and cooked food should be stored separately to avoid cross-contamination of food; 
5. Check the food stored in the refrigerator regularly, and take it out and deal with it in time once it is found that the food has gone bad; 
6. Clean the refrigerator regularly to avoid smudges and odors, which may contaminate food and reduce the service life of the refrigerator;
7. The temperature in different places of the refrigerator is different, so it needs to be stored according to the food type. Bottled food such as drinks and condiments should be put on the bottle holder, leftovers and instant food can be put on the glass shelf in the refrigerator, fruits and vegetables can be put in the crisper, raw meat, seafood and eggs can be stored in the freezer.

1. Before storing food, the refrigerator should run without load for a period of time. After the temperature in the refrigerator drops, food could be put into the refrigerator. Hot foods should be cooled naturally at room temperature before being placed in the refrigerator;
2. When used in summer, the temperature controller should be set at gear 1-3, while in winter, the temperature controller should be set at gear 4-6. Do not set gear 7 unless a lot of food is placed in urgent need of refrigeration;
3. Excessive thickness of ice in the freezer will affect the transfer of cold volume and increase power consumption, so regular deicing is needed to achieve the purpose of electricity saving;
4. The opening of the door will cause the loss of cold air inside the box and increase the power consumption, so try to get food at the same time, reduce the number of times to open and close the door, and try to move quickly to shorten the opening time;
5. Remove obstacles around the refrigerator, maintain good ventilation and heat dissipation conditions, and at the same time, regularly wipe the heating positions on both sides of the refrigerator to ensure good heat dissipation effect.

During daily use, refrigerators are prone to accumulate dirt, odors and bacteria, which can be harmful to our health. Therefore, it is important to clean them thoroughly on a regular basis (once a month is recommended). The steps to clean the refrigerator are as follows:
1. Before cleaning the refrigerator, first turn off the power, take off the power plug, take out all the food stored in the refrigerator;
2. Wipe the outside of the refrigerator first with a soft cloth containing warm water or neutral detergent, and then dry it with a clean soft cloth;
3. Open the door of the box, remove all bottle holders, glass shelves and drawers in the refrigerator and freezer, and then scrub with soft wet cloth and neutral detergent. After scrubbing, wipe with a dry cloth or place in a ventilated place to dry;
4. In order to prevent damage to the coating layer outside the box and the plastic parts inside the box, do not use alkaline or weak alkaline detergent, washing powder, grinding paste, boiled water, acid and organic solvent to clean the refrigerator;
5. Wait for the frost layer in the freezer to melt naturally. During the frost melting period, put a towel at the bottom of the refrigerator to absorb water, so as to prevent excessive water from cleaning. Do not use sharp objects to shovel the frost on the evaporator, otherwise it is easy to scratch the evaporator;
6. After the frost to melt completely, began to scrub the tank freezer, you can use a wet soft cloth with neutral detergent to wipe, but when wiping the refrigerator the components such as switches, floodlight and temperature controller, please twist the soft cloth to dry and then wipe;
7. The door gasket is easy to adhere to dirty things such as soup and juice, which will be easily damaged and lead to cold air leakage after becoming dirty. It is recommended to remove the door gasket and clean it, wipe it dry with a dry cloth, and flatten the door gasket, and heat it evenly with a hair dryer to better restore its elasticity, reinstall the door gasket;
8. After all parts are cleaned, keep the door open. After the refrigerator is fully dried, reinstall the bottle holders, glass shelves, drawers and other accessories;
9. Put the power plug firmly in, check whether the temperature controller is set in the correct position, start the refrigerator, wait for about an hour, check whether the temperature in the box drops, and then put the food into the refrigerator again.

1. First of all, in order to extend the service life of the refrigerator as far as possible and keep the refrigerator in normal working condition, it is not recommended to stop using the refrigerator if there is no special reason after the power is switched on;
2. If you are going out for a short time, you don't have to close the refrigerator, but all the food in the freezer should be taken out to prevent spoilage and contamination of the refrigerator. The food in the freezer (except perishable food) can be kept still;
3. If you need to go out for a long time, it is recommended to stop using the refrigerator. After turning off the power, please take out all the food in the refrigerator. Clean the inside of the refrigerator thoroughly and place it with the door open (to prevent odors).

Stopping the use of the refrigerator will reduce the service life of the refrigerator, accelerate the aging speed of the inner plastic and cause corrosion of the pipeline or parts, so in order to maintain the normal work of the refrigerator, if there is no special reason after starting the power, it is not recommended to stop the refrigerator. If you must stop using it for a period of time for special reasons, please note the following:
1. First, unplug the power plug, take out all the food in the refrigerator, and wait for the frost layer of the freezer to melt completely. Then, fully scrub with a wet soft cloth and neutral detergent, and then rinse with clean water and let dry naturally.
2. After the door gasket is cleaned and dried, it can be coated with lime powder or pad white paper at the contact place between the door gasket and the door body, so as to prevent the door gasket from sticking to the box body. The temperature controller is adjusted to the state of "0" or "MAX", so that the internal spring is in the state of natural relaxation, to extend the service life; 
3. After cleaning the refrigerator, the door should be kept open and placed in a dry and ventilated place away from direct sunlight and heat source. Do not cover the refrigerator with a cover or a plastic bag; 
4. If the refrigerator is not used for a long time, the service life of the refrigerator will be shortened. It is better to power on once a month and turn off the compressor after one hour of normal operation.

1. Wipe the door gasket clean to ensure it is smooth and fit;
2. Refrigerator door gasket falls off or becomes loose (can be directly pressed into the groove by hand);
3. Too much food is placed in the refrigerator or the drawer is not placed in place, which will cause the refrigerator door cannot be closed;
4. Whether the foam bottom of the refrigerator is removed;

1. Turn off the power and unplug the power cord, take out the food stored in the refrigerator, fully clean the refrigerator door, liner, door seals, glass shelves, drawers, bottle holders and other items, dry and open the door to keep ventilation, so as to fully dissipate the internal odor;
2. Clean the refrigerator regularly and deal with the spoiled food in the refrigerator in time;
3. Use plastic wrap or plastic bags to encapsulate food to avoid odor leakage;
4. Put some lemon or tea bags in the refrigerator to get rid of odor;
5. Remove the deodorizer, rinse it with tap water, dry it in the sun and then install and use it.

1. Check whether the power outlet is normal;
2. The voltage is too low, leading to the compressor not running and the refrigerating room not cooling (below 187V);
3. Check whether the gear position of the mechanical refrigerating room is set to 0, leading to no cooling;
4. A small number of mechanical refrigerating rooms have an external temperature compensation switch. When the indoor temperature is lower than 16°C or 10°C, it needs to be turned on manually.

1. Power problem: First, check whether the power cord is damaged and whether the power plug is in good contact. If there is no problem, turn on the power and open the door to see if the light is on.
2. For mechanical refrigerators, when the ambient temperature is lower than the normal starting temperature of the temperature controller, check whether the low-temperature compensation switch of the refrigerator is turned on. Only when the low temperature compensation switch is turned on can the temperature controller be forced on;
3. After starting, observe whether the compressor is working normally, open the rear cover of the compressor and check whether there is pipeline leakage; 
4. It may be that the air duct is blocked or the frost layer of evaporator is too thick, which causes the air not flowing and hinders the transfer of cold quantity. At this time, the air duct should be dredge and the refrigerator should be cleaned;
5. If the problem cannot be solved by the above operation, please contact our professional maintenance personnel.

The temperature of the freezer is very low (about -18 degrees), freezing is normal
1. Manually deicing regularly;
2. It is recommended that food with excessive moisture be packed in a fresh-keeping bag and placed in the box;
3. Frequent opening and closing of the refrigerator door or the door is not closed tightly can also cause the freezing/frosting phenomenon of the freezer.
Note: The freezer of air-cooled refrigerators may have a trace of frost due to the use environment and storage conditions.

1. First, check whether the power cord is damaged and whether the power plug is in good contact. If there is no problem, turn on the power supply and open the box door to see if the light is on；
2. The voltage is too low, causing the compressor to not run (below 187V);
3. Check whether the mechanical refrigerating room gear is set to 0, leading to no cooling, and adjust to other gears or temperature;
4. A small number of mechanical refrigerating rooms have an external temperature compensation switch. When the indoor temperature is lower than 16℃ or 10℃, it needs to be turned on manually.

1. First, check whether the grounding wire is properly connected. If the grounding wire is faulty, please contact professional electrician for maintenance;
2. The insulation failure of the internal circuit of the refrigerator may be caused by poor production if the refrigerator is newly purchased. If it has been used for a period of time, it may be caused by damp corrosion or aging of the internal circuit;
3. Check whether the insulation material outside the power line falls off. If the wire loses insulation protection, it will cause electricity leakage;
4. In case of electric leakage, please contact our professional maintenance personnel for maintenance.

The computer refrigerator with touch screen basically contains the function of child lock. Child lock can avoid children's disorderly press to change the setting of refrigerator at home, causing unnecessary damage and danger. In the child lock mode, all the key operation is invalid.
Methods to unlock the child lock:
1. Long press the temperature zone key for 3 seconds when some models are on the screen;
2. Press the unlock button for 3 seconds to unlock some models;
3. Press the refrigerate and freeze keys for 3 seconds to unlock some models;
4. Different models and slightly different operations, please check the instructions for verification.
